# Debugging & Verification Walkthrough — AI Financial Advisor

We investigated the 500 Internal Server Error encountered on `/dashboard/`, resolved the root cause, tested both existing and new test suites (21 tests total), and verified the full end-to-end user experience in the browser.

---

## 1. Root Cause Analysis & Resolution

### The Bug
When accessing `http://127.0.0.1:5000/dashboard/`, the server returned:
```
werkzeug.routing.exceptions.BuildError: Could not build url for endpoint 'ai.advisor'. Did you mean 'savings.add' instead?
```

### Root Cause
In [`finance_app/app/ai/__init__.py`](file:///c:/Users/nofil/Desktop/Projects/Project/finance_app/app/ai/__init__.py), the blueprint `ai_bp` was defined, but `routes.py` was never imported. Because [`finance_app/app/templates/base.html`](file:///c:/Users/nofil/Desktop/Projects/Project/finance_app/app/templates/base.html#L60) generates navigation links with `url_for('ai.advisor')`, every view rendering `base.html` crashed during Jinja2 URL building.

### Fix
Added `from . import routes  # noqa: E402, F401` to [`finance_app/app/ai/__init__.py`](file:///c:/Users/nofil/Desktop/Projects/Project/finance_app/app/ai/__init__.py):

```diff
  ai_bp = Blueprint('ai', __name__, url_prefix='/ai', template_folder='../templates')
+
+ from . import routes  # noqa: E402, F401
```

